{
  "id": "rem-rebound",
  "term": "REM rebound",
  "definition": "REM rebound is the return of rapid eye movement sleep after it has been selectively deprived, marked by more REM sleep and a shorter delay before REM begins. In this context, it is a biological sleep response that can resemble REM changes seen in depression.",
